{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790264963,"nonce":"/ehVeZAqZyaOqmjZ1q/eURgGvsw=","title":"Lua: a shaped constructor evaluates its positional values after everything else","message":"A constructor with a slotted shape builds its array part as a node the header evaluates, so its positional values run after the keyed field values and computed keys. lua5.4 evaluates fields in source order.\n\n    local log = {}\n    local function f(x) log[#log + 1] = x; return x end\n    local t = {f(\"p1\"), x = f(\"x\"), f(\"p2\")}\n    print(table.concat(log, \",\"))   -- lua5.4 p1,x,p2; zylua x,p1,p2 (main dea6d08b)\n\nThe l2 worktree (f2f2d8c2, setmetatable of a constructor sets meta at birth) extends it to the metatable argument, which is evaluated inside the constructor before the positional values:\n\n    local function g(tag, v) log[#log + 1] = tag; return v end\n    local u = setmetatable({x = 1, f(\"pos\")}, g(\"mt\", {}))   -- lua5.4 pos,mt; l2 mt,pos; main pos,mt\n\nHolding the array part in source order among the other fields fixes both.","files":null}]}